userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: A Fibonacci heap is a collection of min-heap-ordered trees whose roots and whose children are each kept in circular doubly linked lists, and it is exactly this pointer structure that lets operations like insert run in O(1) by splicing a node with a constant number of pointer updates.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): The circular doubly linked lists of roots and of children are the entire secret behind Fibonacci-heap efficiency: insert (and many other operations) only rewire a constant number of neighbor pointers and never rebuild a tree, giving O(1) amortized insertion.
DEMO STEPS: 3 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

FULL BLUEPRINT:
